/target

# Cargo.lock is committed, deliberately.
#
# The usual advice is that a library should not commit one, so that a
# consumer's resolver is free. That advice is about *consumers*, and it
# says nothing about CI — where every job here passes --locked and a
# missing lockfile is not a free resolver, it is a hard failure before
# a single test runs.
#
# This crate has zero dependencies, so the file contains itself and
# nothing else. It constrains no one. What it buys is that --locked
# becomes meaningful: it now also catches a manifest bumped without its
# lockfile, which is a defect two other repositories in this
# organisation shipped this month.
